# Keep image build contexts lean and deterministic (audit S10-F6): dependency
# installs happen inside the image from the lockfile — never copy host installs.

# SEC-1/F3: NEVER ship the operator's real secrets into a build layer. The web
# image is built with `COPY . .` (apps/web/Dockerfile), so an un-ignored `.env`
# — POSTGRES_PASSWORD, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, PS_JWT_SECRET — would be readable in
# that layer by anyone with the image or the build cache, even though the final
# nginx stage only copies `dist`. `.env` is gitignored but git-ignore does NOT
# imply docker-ignore. `.env.example` is deliberately kept (it ships no values).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dev-dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.expo
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
.git
